criteria.title:
System architecture — integration of the eReferral function with the EMR, judged by how patient details reach the referral (not by how the system is built):
(a) Fully integrated = 100% — the eReferral function is part of the EMR, OR it is a standalone system integrated with the EMR whose only role is to perform the referral and which receives the patient details automatically;
(b) Standalone - manual encoding = 50% — the standalone system still requires manual intervention to encode patient details (re-typing, copy-paste or re-upload).

criteria.validator_guide:
Met if ANY one of the following shows that system-only data (user accounts, audit trail, configuration) is backed up per TB-09 and can be restored:
(a) a live restore demonstration in the test environment;
(b) a dated restore-test record (log or report) accepted by the Technical Lead;
(c) a hosting / cloud-provider backup report plus a signed vendor attestation that system-only data is included and restores are tested.
Record the evidence option used in Notes.

Met if compliance with BOTH TB-03 and TB-04 is shown by any accepted evidence option, e.g.:
(a) view-only demonstration of the encryption setting and of the stored form of one TEST password;
(b) configuration screenshots with key values masked;
(c) cloud-provider encryption setting or independent certification covering encryption at rest, plus a signed attestation naming the password-hashing algorithm.
Not Met if any evidence shows plain-text, reversible or MD5 / SHA-1 password storage, or no encryption at rest. Record the evidence option used in Notes.
